# Devstral-2-123B-Instruct-2512, cleaned up for benchmark use.
# https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Devstral-2-123B-Instruct-2512
#
# INSTRUCT-ONLY. No thinking mode -- `ollama show` reports capabilities
# ['completion','tools'] and that is CORRECT here, unlike the Qwen3-32B and
# Qwen3.5-122B builds where a missing "thinking" was a defect. Leave
# AI_ASSISTANT_MODEL_THINK unset for this model or Ollama rejects the request.
#
# Built FROM the blob to clear the inherited SYSTEM block (an empty
# SYSTEM """""" is ignored by ollama create -- verified).
FROM /san/models/blobs/sha256-79068f89c59012e4a174dbfe3f4025a283c961abc201e3499c754b60e3f320ef

# --- TEMPLATE: declared deliberately, unlike the Qwen files ----------------
# This one is CORRECT and must be preserved. It is proper Mistral v7 format --
# [SYSTEM_PROMPT], [INST], [TOOL_CALLS], [TOOL_RESULTS], </s> -- so there is
# nothing to fix, and building FROM the blob would discard it in favour of
# whatever the GGUF does or does not carry. Reproduced verbatim from the
# existing build rather than gambling on re-derivation.
TEMPLATE """{{- range $index, $_ := .Messages }}
{{- if eq .Role "system" }}[SYSTEM_PROMPT]{{ .Content }}[/SYSTEM_PROMPT]
{{- else if eq .Role "user" }}
{{- if and (le (len (slice $.Messages $index)) 2) $.Tools }}[AVAILABLE_TOOLS]{{ $.Tools }}[/AVAILABLE_TOOLS]
{{- end }}[INST]{{ .Content }}[/INST]
{{- else if eq .Role "assistant" }}
{{- if .Content }}{{ .Content }}
{{- if not (eq (len (slice $.Messages $index)) 1) }}</s>
{{- end }}
{{- else if .ToolCalls }}[TOOL_CALLS][
{{- range .ToolCalls }}{"name": "{{ .Function.Name }}", "arguments": {{ .Function.Arguments }}}
{{- end }}]</s>
{{- end }}
{{- else if eq .Role "tool" }}[TOOL_RESULTS]{"content": {{ .Content }}}[/TOOL_RESULTS]
{{- end }}
{{- end }}"""

# --- Stops: seven removed --------------------------------------------------
# The existing build carried these, none of which are Mistral tokens:
#   </thinking>  </tool_call>  </tool_response>  </ask_followup_question>
#   </attempt_completion>  </write_to_file>  </execute_command>
# They are Cline / Roo-Code agentic tool tags -- this tag was set up to drive a
# coding agent, not to write prose reviews. "</thinking>" is the same shape of
# trap that made MiniMax-M2.7 return empty content: a stop string the model
# emits mid-answer ends generation on the spot. Devstral is instruct-only so
# it likely never fired, but nothing here should be able to truncate a review.
#
# Kept: </s> is the genuine Mistral EOS and appears in the template above.
# [/TOOL_RESULTS] is a Mistral control token the assistant should never emit;
# harmless as a defensive stop.
PARAMETER stop "</s>"
PARAMETER stop "[/TOOL_RESULTS]"

# --- Samplers --------------------------------------------------------------
# The card prescribes no sampler row at all -- its examples only ever set
# temperature 0.15. So there is no "card value" to align to.
#
# What the build DID carry was temperature 0.6 / top_k 20 / top_p 0.8. That is
# the exact triple found on Qwen3-32B and Qwen3-Coder-Next, i.e. contamination
# from a Qwen Modelfile rather than anything chosen for a Mistral model.
# Replacing it with neutral values so that temperature -- which the harness
# controls -- is the only thing shaping the distribution.
PARAMETER top_p 1.0
PARAMETER top_k 0
PARAMETER min_p 0

# Left at the existing 1.1. The card specifies no repetition_penalty, and
# unlike top_p/top_k this value is not obviously copied from the Qwen builds
# (they use 1.05), so there is no evidence to justify moving it.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# --- Inert for benchmark runs, kept for `ollama run` and other callers -----
# The workflow always sends temperature / num_ctx / num_predict in options.
# 0.15 is the value used throughout the card's examples.
#
# num_ctx set to the benchmark's 65536, down from 131072. The GGUF reports
# mistral3.context_length 262144 and the card says 256k native, so this is a
# deliberate reduction for KV-cache reasons on a 123B, not a limit -- the
# opposite of Qwen3-32B, where 40960 is a hard ceiling being exceeded.
PARAMETER temperature 0.15
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536

# --- No SYSTEM block ------------------------------------------------------
# Previously: "You are a helpful assistant".
#
# The card does recommend a system prompt, but the one it ships is for a
# different job: "You are operating as and within Mistral Vibe, a CLI
# coding-agent...". That is agentic-CLI framing, not code review, and this tag
# is also consumed by the patcher. Task framing belongs in review_prompt.md and
# the patcher prompt, which are SHA-tracked in every scorecard; a Modelfile
# SYSTEM appears nowhere in the artefact.

# --- Standard SYSTEM prompt (fleet-wide) ----------------------------------
# Identical on every model in the benchmark, so the system prompt stops being an
# uncontrolled variable. Before this, the fleet ran a mix: "/no_think Be concise
# and skip chain-of-thought" on the six Qwen3.x builds, an expert-engineer
# persona on Qwen3-Coder-30B, a "detailed answers" persona on Qwen3.5-122B and
# Qwen3-32B, "Reasoning strength: high" on Muse-Glimmer-30B, and nothing at all
# on Gemma-4-31B -- none of it recorded in any scorecard.
#
# A non-empty SYSTEM replaces an inherited one, so this works whether the FROM
# line points at a blob or a tag. Keep it byte-identical across every model:
# the moment one differs, cross-model comparison is confounded again.
#
# Task instructions do NOT belong here -- they live in review_prompt.md, which
# is SHA-tracked in every scorecard. This line is persona only.
SYSTEM """You are an expert computer programmer with an eye for detail, who loves to provide high quality answers."""
